WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.030
A long straight wall.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.090
Forty metres of fencing.

3
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.870
The fence makes three
sides of a rectangular pen.

4
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.240
The wall makes the fourth.

5
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.190
Five metres out and thirty along gives
one hundred and fifty square metres.

6
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.780
Make it a square, thirteen
and a third metres each way.

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.730
The area grows to about one hundred
and seventy-seven point eight.

8
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.060
Same fence, different areas.

9
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.280
So which rectangle encloses the most?

10
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.310
In this mission, you'll write
the area using one length, x.

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.010
A equals x times, forty minus two x.

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.900
You'll see the area rise, then fall,
and use differentiation to find the top,

13
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.870
where the gradient is zero.

14
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.620
Your mission: find the rectangle that
encloses the most area with forty metres

15
00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.040
of fence and a wall.
